List the unpowered polarity inspections in "pre_power", one per polarised part
above. For a part with an ISSUE, the inspection must name the issue and say
what reading confirms it, so a reversed part is caught before power, not by
the supply collapsing. Then order the powered checks so each one is a landmark: say what you expect to see BEFORE
measuring. Start with the negative test: force the failure condition (e.g.
block the beam, disconnect a wire) and confirm the board reports it. A sensor
that only ever reports success is following the map backwards.

Return only JSON:
